    "dd1362": [
      {
        "id": 1,
        "lang": "lg-nolan",
        "value": "<p>Use the JSON version exported by Zotero to import into Publications section: rsc205</p><p>The config of the tool defines the map between Zotero and Dédalo.</p><p> </p><p>Control of section_id with a Zotero field:</p><p> </p><p>By default, the tool uses the Zotero field 'call-number' to define the section_id of the record: Zotero has no editable id, so write the record number there. When the call-number is a whole number (1 to 2147483647, digits only), Dédalo updates the record with that section_id, or creates it at that id when it does not exist (also when it was deleted). An item whose call-number is anything else is not imported, and the report names it. A record that already holds a different Zotero key is never overwritten: that item is refused, and so is an item whose Zotero key is held by another record than its call-number names, or a call-number repeated in the same import. Without a call-number, the reference is matched by its Zotero key (the last part of its Zotero URI), stored in the component the map's 'id' entry names (Code, rsc137): a re-import updates the record that holds the key, a new key creates a record. It's possible to set another field to control the section_id with the Zotero file. To do that, create a specific config in \"Development->tools->Tool configuration\" section and change \"field_to_section_id\" to the name of the Zotero field with the section_id (it names a Zotero field, no component is bound to it). You can see the default config in the register tool or in 'sample_config.json'. Specific configuration need to be a full configuration, not only the property changed.</p><p> </p><p>Upload PDF files:</p><p> </p><p>It is possible to upload PDF files with the Zotero records. By default the tool uses Zotero 'archive' field set with the full name of the PDF file.</p><p> </p><p>\"archive\" : \"my_pdf_file.pdf\"</p><p> </p><p>Add the PDF files with the Zotero json file in the tool, upload all and import.</p>"
      }
    ],
